 granted. We will deal with the first one first. We will call it No. 2 on sheet 7110. Nick Xenophon For the sake of completeness, I should move amendment (1), which is a consequential amendment that relates to the commencement of part 3 of the act and states that it commences 'The day after this Act receives Royal Assent'. I should move that along with— Stephen Parry Senator Xenophon, if I could just interject there, we will deal with that afterwards as that is consequential. We will deal with the two amendments that we have just highlighted, if you are comfortable to deal with it that way. Nick Xenophon I do not think that it is possible for you to interject from your position. Nick Sherry It's disorderly! Stephen Parry Can I offer a direction in that regard. Nick Xenophon I was not suggesting that what you were doing was disorderly, Mr Chairman. I am suggesting that you are giving me a direction rather than an interjection. Stephen Parry And, if you accept that direction, we will go ahead and deal with amendment (2). Nick Xenophon I wholeheartedly accept that direction and I move amendment (2) on sheet 7110: (2) Schedule 1, page 25 (after line 20), at the end of the Schedule, add: Part 3—Amendments relating to termination fees and credit fees and charges _Banking Act 1959_ 1 At the end subsection 9(4) Add \"or the requirements of section 9AF\". 2 Af","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-2016","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2011-07-04/2"}
